 "_": [
  "NOT ON MACOS FLEET PEERS: 'Set password' on a desktop caches the password-derived key in",
  "the OS keychain (enable_password_protection with require_on_launch false, flags 0x03). A macOS",
  "peer started over ssh-to-self has no keychain, and macOS put a 'Keychain Not Found' modal",
  "(Cancel / Reset To Defaults) on the person's screen (2026-10-18). Run it on Windows peers",
  "(windows:<letter> from the Mac), after copying the flutter_secure_storage.dat aside as",
  "regress_app_lock says.",
  "",
  "B4 + B5 on the macOS desktop backend, two THROWAWAY peers k and l: two profiles (two data",
  "roots) on ONE macOS account, so they share the keychain flutter_secure_storage writes to.",
  "k sets an app password and a wider-scope duress code; while k holds its launch secret, the",
  "'this computer only' note stays away. l sets its own password and turns Ask before Hollow",
  "starts ON, which deletes l's launch secret. Before B4 that was ONE shared entry, so k lost",
  "its silent start and the note appeared on k. Then B5's pacing at k's lock prompt: four",
  "misses say Wrong, the fifth makes the prompt wait 30 s, after which the password opens it.",
  "Both passwords are turned off at the end, which clears each profile's entries.",
  "run: from the Mac, Windows peers per the hollow-runner skill (never FLEET_BACKEND=macos)"
 ],
